\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-REL-01]\\n\\n# Release: v1.39.0 — Release v1.39.0/v0.61.0/v0.15.0/v0.0.14\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/releases/tag/v1.39.0  \\n\\n**Author**: MrAlias  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-12-08T16:32:32Z · **Updated**: 2025-12-08T16:45:46Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**Tag**: `v1.39.0`  \\n\\n**Published**: 2025-12-08T16:45:46Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\n### Added\\n\\n- Greatly reduce the cost of recording metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric` using hashing for map keys. (#7175)\\n\\n- Add `WithInstrumentationAttributeSet` option to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/log`, `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/metric`, and `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/trace` packages. This provides a concurrent-safe and performant alternative to `WithInstrumentationAttributes` by accepting a pre-constructed `attribute.Set`. (#7287)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability for the Prometheus exporter in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus`. Check the `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/prometheus/internal/x` package documentation for more information. (#7345)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlplog/otlploggrpc`. (#7353)\\n\\n- Add temporality selector functions `DeltaTemporalitySelector`, `CumulativeTemporalitySelector`, `LowMemoryTemporalitySelector` to `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/metric`. (#7434)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for simple log processor in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/log`. (#7548)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracegrpc`. (#7459)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/exporters/otlp/otlptrace/otlptracehttp`. (#7486)\\n\\n- Add experimental observability metrics for simple span processor in `go.opentelemetry.io/otel/sdk/trace`. (#7374)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src rel 01 releas v1 39 0 releas v1 39 0 v0 61 0 v0 15 0 v0 0 14 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go releas tag v1 39 0 author mralia creat 2025 12 08t16 32 32z updat 2025 12 08t16 45 46z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z tag v1 39 0 publish 2025 12 08t16 45 46z overview ad great reduc the cost of record metric in go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric use hash for map key 7175 add withinstrumentationattributeset option to go opentelemetri io otel log go opentelemetri io otel metric and go opentelemetri io otel trace packag this provid a concurr safe and perform altern to withinstrumentationattribut by accept a pre construct attribut set 7287 add experiment observ for the prometheus export in go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus check the go opentelemetri io otel export prometheus intern x packag document for more inform 7345 add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlplog otlploggrpc 7353 add tempor selector function deltatemporalityselector cumulativetemporalityselector lowmemorytemporalityselector to go opentelemetri io otel sdk metric 7434 add experiment observ metric for simpl log processor in go opentelemetri io otel sdk log 7548 add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlptrac otlptracegrpc 7459 add experiment observ metric in go opentelemetri io otel export otlp otlptrac otlptracehttp 7486 add experiment observ metric for simpl span processor in go opentelemetri io otel sdk trace 7374\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"id\": \"a1aa75b09f729579\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3743555851708863, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.20581712167269475, \"vector_similarity\": 0.767612, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8765f6c08a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/releases/release-v1.39.0.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 52878, \"chunk_count\": 30, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:09:56\", \"token_count\": 15994, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/71382)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455](https://github.com/golang/go/issues/74455)\\n\\n*   **Bryan Boreham** questioned the relevance to OpenTelemetry, to which Damien clarified it's for instrumenting file uploads via the HTTP server.\\n\\n*   The discussion revolved around implementing an automatic cleanup mechanism for these temporary files. Proposed solutions included:\\n\\n    *   Option 1: `c.Request.MultipartForm.RemoveAll()`\\n\\n    *   Option 2: Leave it to the user to decide (\\\"whoever uses it is responsible for cleanup\\\")\\n\\n    *   Option 3: Provide a configurable option with a default.\\n\\n*   Damien suggested starting with automatic deletion without an explicit option, adding one only if a strong need arises. The notes from the agenda suggested starting with default behavior of removal, waiting for user interest to add configuration, and empowering component owners to make this decision.\\n\\n*   Tyler acknowledged that the instrumentation is responsible for cleanup and that this issue needs to be addressed.\\n\\n**3. Long-seen Code Owners/Triagers Check-in**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** reported that Chengzhen (Scorpion Knives), a triager and code owner for otelzap and otelecho, has had no GitHub activity since February and is the sole owner for otelecho.\\n\\n*   Damien pinged Chengzhen on Slack today and will wait a couple of weeks for a response. If there's no response, he plans to propose moving Chengzhen to Emeritus status due to inactivity.\\n\\n**4. Robert Pająk's PR (Parsing Algorithm)**\\n\\n*   **Robert Pająk** asked Tyler if his PR ([sdk/log: Fix AddAttributes, SetAttributes, SetBody on Record to not mutate input #7403](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/pull/7403)) needed Tyler's specific review or if another approval would suffice to unblock it.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** encouraged others to review and stated that the project shouldn't be blocked waiting for him, though he would try to review it within a few days.\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** offered to review the PR. The goal is to merge it into the current milestone.\\n\\n**5. David Ashpole's PRs (Metrics SDK Optimizations)**\\n\\n*   **David Ashpole** provided an update on his histogram reservoir optimization PR. He explained that fixing a race condition initially worsened performance, making it equivalent to using a lock. The new approach involves one lock per measurement instead of one for the whole reservoir, resulting in a 3x-4x performance improvement. The PR is now much simpler and mostly involves concurrent safety testing.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 71382 http github com golang go issu 74455 http github com golang go issu 74455 bryan boreham question the relev to opentelemetri to which damien clarifi it s for instrument file upload via the http server the discuss revolv around implement an automat cleanup mechan for these temporari file propos solut includ option 1 c request multipartform removeal option 2 leav it to the user to decid whoever us it is respons for cleanup option 3 provid a configur option with a default damien suggest start with automat delet without an explicit option ad one onli if a strong need aris the note from the agenda suggest start with default behavior of remov wait for user i